            {
                "entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                "word": "imfall",
                "pos": "particle",
                "lang_code": "de",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "glosses": [
                            "nur dass du es weißt / nur dass Sie es wissen; nebenbei bemerkt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Swiss Standard German"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90772a76-2b64-43de-add8-eae85897a28e",
                                "sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                                "text": "„In welchem Fall? Im Falle eines Falles? Nein, einfach so, imfall. Eine unverfroren selbstgerechte Art, ein angebrachtes Argument zu betonen. Nur so, imfall.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db72e3e6-26b4-41a6-87f1-37b89ed16d2d",
                                "sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                                "text": "„Okay, es gibt da doch noch eine zusätzliche Zeit: die «Gango-Form». Passt für Handlungen in der Gegenwart wie auch in der Zukunft. «Ich gahn go Tennis spiele», oder «ich gahn in Chäller go Gonfi hole». Ob daher auch der Ausdruck «Ich bin imfall nöd din Gango!» kommt?“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4edf0bd-fd83-4191-9039-4e11c9354ebb",
                                "sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                                "text": "«Das bi dänn imfall ich!» (hochdeutsch: „Das bin dann übrigens ich!“)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d57990d4-cb68-4a1a-ace4-7eaf19388325",
                                "sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                                "text": "Ein Wort verleiht jeder Aussage mehr Gewicht – imfall!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8066d993-3f95-4eef-94ec-400a9b0909e1",
                                "sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                                "text": "beschwichtigend: „Das war imfall nicht bös gemeint.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e1f76516-bb08-4a96-bf70-1e98e3178704",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "target_lang_word": "by the way",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "by the way",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cffdfdc4-0a90-3fc6-b3b0-5b6a0c36a0c1",
                                        "entry_id": "5a0237cf-352a-3c90-a1e0-cabe4f944ff2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Incidentally; used in referencing a parenthetical statement not timely, central, or crucial to the topic at hand; foregone, passed by, something that has already happened."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "960ecbc3-56f7-4c24-a0ce-6006a5680d9e",
                                                "sense_id": "cffdfdc4-0a90-3fc6-b3b0-5b6a0c36a0c1",
                                                "text": "His mother will be coming for dinner tomorrow, and, by the way, she recently sold her collection of ceramic eggs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0b9a8e6-11ac-4afd-aa51-a9b9a3504884",
                                                "sense_id": "cffdfdc4-0a90-3fc6-b3b0-5b6a0c36a0c1",
                                                "text": "[…] I had counted on a life-lease of the profits, whereas I only received those of a few short years. But this is by the way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99bddfa7-1eaf-4659-8deb-12c6b75cdd10",
                                                "sense_id": "cffdfdc4-0a90-3fc6-b3b0-5b6a0c36a0c1",
                                                "text": "“A very welcome, kind, useful present, that means to the parish. By the way, Hopkins, let this go no further. We don't want the tale running round that a rich person has arrived. Churchill, my dear fellow, we have such greedy sharks, and wolves in lamb's clothing.[…]”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "by the way",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7c86ccf-5468-39af-b0e2-2d5cd5d76cc3",
                                        "entry_id": "e2f36a7d-732d-3fcc-a5ec-7cff983d603c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Irrelevantly, off-topic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "472584d6-2606-47df-ad19-232d65c488f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "target_lang_word": "for the record",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "for the record",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b9663c4-de9f-3472-b4b1-2416821e7754",
                                        "entry_id": "c875c3af-715a-3151-8665-78028c0b2fbb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For the purpose of being recorded, especially when already known."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3f9d41a-8feb-460a-9e63-3ea5cf7bf9e8",
                                                "sense_id": "8b9663c4-de9f-3472-b4b1-2416821e7754",
                                                "text": "I will ask you, for the record, to state your name and address."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ec50fb3-a2c7-499f-8e03-351dd36e3a0c",
                                                "sense_id": "8b9663c4-de9f-3472-b4b1-2416821e7754",
                                                "text": "Now, just for the record, you have served time for drug dealing, haven't you?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a7d07cd-5946-4b70-ac43-4e700cba8203",
                                                "sense_id": "8b9663c4-de9f-3472-b4b1-2416821e7754",
                                                "text": "During brief courtroom appearances, Pattan restricted his comments for the record to “Guilty, sir” for each of the two counts of the indictment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6256cbcb-3f63-3ea5-9272-ae3d47d6b264",
                                        "entry_id": "c875c3af-715a-3151-8665-78028c0b2fbb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For the purpose of following correct procedure, especially when otherwise redundant and repetitive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "697f2b87-cf6a-4393-a475-43403a9b83e2",
                                                "sense_id": "6256cbcb-3f63-3ea5-9272-ae3d47d6b264",
                                                "text": "The court almost certainly knows your answer to this already, but, for the record, do you plea guilty or not guilty?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a6b6105-2484-4d76-b2b2-7ffd0dddd5d9",
                                                "sense_id": "6256cbcb-3f63-3ea5-9272-ae3d47d6b264",
                                                "text": "I can definitely send you those documents, but you'll need to send the request in writing just for the record."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa26b2fa-f183-3e69-91cf-55d0c5553d30",
                                        "entry_id": "c875c3af-715a-3151-8665-78028c0b2fbb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to emphasize a point in an attempt to make it known or noticed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0348d7b7-7744-4b35-a4b7-43a85ec27c08",
                                                "sense_id": "aa26b2fa-f183-3e69-91cf-55d0c5553d30",
                                                "text": "For the record, I think these policies are weird and unnecessary."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5e8cda6-d934-4eec-9e64-b7666df94085",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "target_lang_word": "anyway",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anyway",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "624e8085-dc54-3de9-8cb7-ad48ea71c66d",
                                        "entry_id": "ccd67228-325c-304e-80b6-0187c9512dac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Regardless; anyhow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f68e5d33-bd50-425e-9ce7-f8fd5ae95f88",
                                                "sense_id": "624e8085-dc54-3de9-8cb7-ad48ea71c66d",
                                                "text": "He didn't enjoy washing his car, but it was so dirty that he did it anyway."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3963f60-b255-4b57-b1c3-2acb6069e309",
                                                "sense_id": "624e8085-dc54-3de9-8cb7-ad48ea71c66d",
                                                "text": "Raymond Carver had only moments late at night to write after grueling day jobs, tense relationships, putting kids to bed, and dealing with his own alcoholism. And he wrote anyway."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a96c8d4-d45f-3937-b84d-55451e27e6ea",
                                        "entry_id": "ccd67228-325c-304e-80b6-0187c9512dac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See anyhow and at least."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c696683-8c5f-4694-9d43-15e4778dd3af",
                                                "sense_id": "4a96c8d4-d45f-3937-b84d-55451e27e6ea",
                                                "text": "I don't think that's true. I haven't found any evidence, anyway."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "352438d5-acfa-4ba0-adae-e69023ff619a",
                                                "sense_id": "4a96c8d4-d45f-3937-b84d-55451e27e6ea",
                                                "text": "But I wish there were somethin’ you would do or say\nTo try and make me change my mind and stay\nWe never did too much talkin’ anyway\nDon’t think twice, it’s all right."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ef4644b-5caf-3353-aceb-ba8b7e78d3de",
                                        "entry_id": "ccd67228-325c-304e-80b6-0187c9512dac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to indicate a change of subject."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa6b4851-64b8-4e21-90d4-3d445866fccc",
                                                "sense_id": "4ef4644b-5caf-3353-aceb-ba8b7e78d3de",
                                                "text": "\"I'll be ninety my next birthday, but Louella doesn't tell her age. Anyway, we're going to have you and Cynthia up for supper.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c6fa63c-7c76-35a8-abad-644040b4a8dc",
                                        "entry_id": "ccd67228-325c-304e-80b6-0187c9512dac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used at the end of a question for emphasis, or to direct the conversation to something of more broad importance (compare with more to the point)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "651cd099-071c-4858-bc65-79c5729bd100",
                                                "sense_id": "5c6fa63c-7c76-35a8-abad-644040b4a8dc",
                                                "text": "“But I say, Kid, isn't that going it a little too strong? Whisky and alcohol's bad enough; but when it comes to brandy and pepper-sauce and—” ¶ “Dump it in. Who's making this punch, anyway?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b0ee069-380b-4d13-bdbd-6e5817fc9b71",
                                                "sense_id": "5c6fa63c-7c76-35a8-abad-644040b4a8dc",
                                                "text": "The name, Barry Frank, the name of the game when it comes to money these days, in every sport, is television revenue. How do they get enough money- let me back up a minute. How did the United States get the World Cup anyway? Of all the countries in the world, you'd think we'd be the last one to get it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c61dbab8-c44b-4b62-ad1c-ced5b99ad7c5",
                                                "sense_id": "5c6fa63c-7c76-35a8-abad-644040b4a8dc",
                                                "text": "“We should probably wait until Luke gets here to talk about it,” Leia suggested quietly before Han could answer. Lando glanced past Han, as if only just noticing Luke's absence. “Where is he, anyway?”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba4e186f-cc78-3bba-8668-19f467c702bc",
                                        "entry_id": "ccd67228-325c-304e-80b6-0187c9512dac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In any way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eef9dd90-d944-40d4-87e1-696337e7574e",
                                                "sense_id": "ba4e186f-cc78-3bba-8668-19f467c702bc",
                                                "text": "He that sleeps in the day-time, or is in suspense, fear, anyway troubled in mind, or goes to bed upon a full stomach, may never hope for quiet rest in the night […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dbce6c23-a41c-4f5e-ad9f-1f8bb88ae116",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "target_lang_word": "in any case",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "in any case",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                        "entry_id": "af849dda-7a81-3b95-88c5-b02b328fd489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Whatever be the case."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5af30d00-9865-4f22-a5c9-844c150ca21b",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "Who knows how many more inches of snow will fall tonight, but in any case, we can expect to be doing a lot of shoveling tomorrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f040ec8d-3f13-4b49-94d7-ebf0a2060053",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "Later Martin said, \"If we ever have another baby girl, I'm going to give her a simple name like Mary Jane.\" When we did have another daughter, we called her Bernice Albertine, after her two grandmothers. Not quite Mary Jane, but at least named for members of the family. In any case, she is known as Bunny,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c48be66b-bd0d-416f-ac2f-17c35390cfd1",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "The Information Department is outhoused but there are operational reasons for this and it would, in any case, be physically impossible to house the staff of the Department in the main building."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31550733-bd5e-4d79-878e-5ee97603a773",
                                                "sense_id": "453cbeb0-1473-3adc-950c-d17ded0cea67",
                                                "text": "Because of the juristic difficulties associated with the Donation of Constantine, the question of whether the papacy had in any case prescribed its jurisdiction in the patrimony had become a common topic amongst jurists […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ffe5d7a-0214-39b4-8ce1-a67def60f157",
                                        "entry_id": "af849dda-7a81-3b95-88c5-b02b328fd489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see in, any, case."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e44218ce-c91c-4eff-8492-ecca98ed7e40",
                                                "sense_id": "9ffe5d7a-0214-39b4-8ce1-a67def60f157",
                                                "text": "Their most popular product, an assortment of ales, is packaged such that there are always at least two bottles of India pale ale in any case."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c8c2f90e-37e6-4837-a058-d852a4c38832",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "target_lang_word": "definitely",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "definitely",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "335c0432-ecda-3b42-83e3-253cbb297a38",
                                        "entry_id": "3a09d650-9e94-3015-b0e8-e1845b55f8ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without question and beyond doubt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17663ba8-eeae-4fe3-9e67-4374926ada7f",
                                                "sense_id": "335c0432-ecda-3b42-83e3-253cbb297a38",
                                                "text": "Joe definitely doesn't know how to drive a tractor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35bac096-e678-43d3-8b69-e38e3bbec1d9",
                                                "sense_id": "335c0432-ecda-3b42-83e3-253cbb297a38",
                                                "text": "She said she wasn't coming, definitely."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbc49c65-7966-3a49-bd7b-c0811295f06d",
                                        "entry_id": "3a09d650-9e94-3015-b0e8-e1845b55f8ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a definite manner; decisively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8183e1b2-41c5-49da-ad93-89cff4ff9f2a",
                                                "sense_id": "dbc49c65-7966-3a49-bd7b-c0811295f06d",
                                                "text": "It was really impossible on board that ship to get away definitely from Almayer"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64f95043-a2cb-43a6-811e-598be8b23344",
                                                "sense_id": "dbc49c65-7966-3a49-bd7b-c0811295f06d",
                                                "text": "And the Nose definitely turned away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b77493ff-1187-43e1-8a19-bdf51e9f198f",
                                                "sense_id": "dbc49c65-7966-3a49-bd7b-c0811295f06d",
                                                "text": "And these Elders were men of good standing in that community, and they swore definitely before the counsel that this lady committed this impropriety, and there was nobody to gainsay that, except the lady herself, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "28cc81da-a556-4132-80bf-3b3dd6acc8fb",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "target_lang_word": "de toute façon",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "de toute façon",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4e7868-2717-316c-947f-2ca46e2d4d27",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "De quelque façon que cela soit ; dans tous les cas ; quelle que soit la situation ; utilisé pour passer outre ou qualifier la notion précédente, ou pour indiquer qu'une affirmation est vraie peu importe l'existence de la notion précédente."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa4815fb-ed2b-4029-b81f-3ccc82fdd37c",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "4 avril 1871. Ils n'ont encore rien compris. De toute façon les vaincus, ça n'a pas besoin de comprendre. Ça doit accepter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd1e0f56-de1b-4101-beef-5588f54ecbd9",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "Le téléphone avait sonné plusieurs fois, des cons qu'elle n’avait pu s’empêcher d’envoyer aux pelotes, quelle importance puisque de toute façon, sans le moineau, l’émission était foutue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "626d3a64-c458-4ba5-a474-45ec3de30524",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "J'aimerais que vous sacrifiiez un haut-parleur, et donc les quelques euros qu'il vous aura coûté. De toute façon, ce sacrifice ne sera pas inutile, car pour comprendre comment fonctionne un composant, rien de mieux que de le démonter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43347be7-2d95-4465-9d21-77da487a8959",
                                                "sense_id": "21e6a8af-e5ec-3b6b-97f7-c1553e7b5cdd",
                                                "text": "— Moi non plus, je n'ai plus de cigarettes, dit-il.\n— Putain de votre race à tous, dit Louise. J'en ai dans mon bungalow au Sun, je vais les chercher. De toute façon, fallait que je m'habille."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4f6e3be2-df02-409a-bc69-dfcce59ce655",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4d64e3d-ce90-37ac-a234-cd4f155c5576",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f3eb332-c907-3c65-a830-14ed21003502",
                        "target_lang_word": "en passant",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "en passant",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7580ce3d-0a85-3aa9-90e8-139fb1fdc78c",
                                        "entry_id": "8f66eeb2-a967-36bb-89f0-053f840638c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En faisant avec quelque sorte de précipitation et sans y avoir donné le temps nécessaire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce26b0e5-0fa2-46f4-9f91-1d237f566b24",
                                                "sense_id": "7580ce3d-0a85-3aa9-90e8-139fb1fdc78c",
                                                "text": "Je n’ai pas eu le loisir d’examiner l’endroit, je ne l’ai vu qu’en passant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e61dcc1-c9c4-49fe-bdae-cba42d441375",
                                                "sense_id": "7580ce3d-0a85-3aa9-90e8-139fb1fdc78c",
                                                "text": "Je ne lui ai parlé de votre affaire qu’en passant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe87bf55-d1e2-464e-b9a6-1b8a731bfd5c",
                                                "sense_id": "7580ce3d-0a85-3aa9-90e8-139fb1fdc78c",
                                                "text": "J’ai traité cet appel comme n’importe quel autre, sans enjeu d’aucune sorte, un petit signe en passant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a192a29c-0e1f-35c7-af28-082159c24050",
                                        "entry_id": "8f66eeb2-a967-36bb-89f0-053f840638c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Se dit, en interrompant le fil d’une conversation, pour parler succinctement d’une chose qui se présente à l’esprit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85e1e6b1-acc3-4f9d-b790-9dd0afaa3658",
                                                "sense_id": "a192a29c-0e1f-35c7-af28-082159c24050",
                                                "text": "Nous dirons en passant que les céréales sont beaucoup moins sujettes à la verse en Champagne que dans d'autres contrées."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5ed221b-b9d9-42e8-8ea1-80fa3aa1242b",
                                                "sense_id": "a192a29c-0e1f-35c7-af28-082159c24050",
                                                "text": "Un peu de ridicule et de bizarrerie se mêle infailliblement à cette époque transitoire de l’âge des garçons, et il me faut bien indiquer cette note en passant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dd02069-9bcd-4fb9-823f-6a7d19d92682",
                                                "sense_id": "a192a29c-0e1f-35c7-af28-082159c24050",
                                                "text": "Je mentionne, en passant, les méfaits du micronationalisme."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
